From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 23:30:16 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 17/21] PCI: qcom: gate the shutdown() action behind
 pcie_qcom.shutdown_l2

The previous commit (pw 1211123 v9 4/4) gives the driver a shutdown()
callback that masks the Global and chained MSI IRQs and forces the link
into L2 before reboot / power-off cut the controller's clocks, against
SMMU translation faults and NoC errors from transactions in flight.

Make it opt-in: with pcie_qcom.shutdown_l2=0 (default, read-only) the
callback returns at once, as the driver had no shutdown action before;
1 runs it. The dw_pcie_suspend_noirq() force argument and
dw_pcie_mask_msi() of the two commits before are unused by default
(every existing caller passes force=false).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/pci/controller/dwc/pcie-qcom.c | 13 ++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/pci/controller/dwc/pcie-qcom.c b/drivers/pci/controller/dwc/pcie-qcom.c
index 0b3a54dadcc04..c766c303a236a 100644
--- a/drivers/pci/controller/dwc/pcie-qcom.c
+++ b/drivers/pci/controller/dwc/pcie-qcom.c
@@ -327,6 +327,13 @@ MODULE_PARM_DESC(parf_halt_off, "iceland: 1 = PARF AXI halt features off where t
 static bool suspend_linkoff;
 module_param(suspend_linkoff, bool, 0444);
 MODULE_PARM_DESC(suspend_linkoff, "iceland: 1 = Kaanapali link to L2 and off in system suspend (default 0; not with WoWLAN)");
+/*
+ * shutdown_l2 - mask the controller IRQs and force the link to L2 at shutdown / reboot (pw 1211123 v9 4/4);
+ *               0 keeps the driver without a shutdown action, as before
+ */
+static bool shutdown_l2;
+module_param(shutdown_l2, bool, 0444);
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(shutdown_l2, "iceland: 1 = link to L2 and controller IRQs masked at shutdown / reboot (default 0)");
 
 struct qcom_pcie_perst {
 	struct list_head list;
@@ -2550,8 +2557,12 @@ static int qcom_pcie_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 static void qcom_pcie_shutdown(struct platform_device *pdev)
 {
 	struct qcom_pcie *pcie = platform_get_drvdata(pdev);
-	struct dw_pcie *pci = pcie->pci;
+	struct dw_pcie *pci;
+
+	if (!shutdown_l2 || !pcie)
+		return;
 
+	pci = pcie->pci;
 	if (pcie->global_irq)
 		disable_irq(pcie->global_irq);
 
